2. Platform-as-a-Service Approach (AWS Elastic Beanstalk / Render / Railway)

Instead of managing the underlying OS, you package your project directories.
• Elastic Beanstalk Configuration: Put a Procfile into your backend deployment root zip archive to instruct the platform how to fire your node thread.
procfile
web: node dist/server.js
Use code with caution.
• Environment Configuration: Inject database strings (DATABASE_URL, MONGO_URI) through the platform dashboard UI. This keeps passwords out of version control and prevents leaking configurations to public repositories.

